      <groundspeak:short_description html="True">&lt;b&gt;16 September 2026, 17:45 - 19:45&lt;/b&gt;</groundspeak:short_description>
      <groundspeak:long_description html="True">&lt;p&gt;An ongoing monthly Geocaching Dinner Event in Lincoln, open to everyone, especially good for geocachers new to the game. It&amp;#39;s a great way to get tips and tricks, or help. Local and out-of-town geocachers are welcome and encouraged to attend. No 4-legged cachers here, sorry. Unless it&amp;#39;s a service dog, then that&amp;#39;s okay. No purchase is required to attend this event. Come join us for a nice suppertime get-together. This will be a great opportunity to plan a weekend geocaching trip with other cachers, ask for help on those caches or puzzle caches that are driving you crazy, trade/share Travel Bugs and/or other trackable items, or just have a nice dinner and trade geocaching stories or talk about whatever. Location: The Eatery, 2548 S. 48th Street, Lincoln Date: Wednesday, September 16th Start Time: 5:45 pm / End Time: 7:45 pm (end time varies, but restaurant closes at 8:00) We will have the party room, so if you’ll please log a Will Attend I can tell them an approximate number to expect they will be sure to have appropriate staff on hand to take care of us!&lt;/p&gt;
</groundspeak:long_description>
      <groundspeak:encoded_hints>In the party room.</groundspeak:encoded_hints>
